# Reviewed findings that are not secrets. One line per fingerprint, each with the
# reason — an unexplained entry here is indistinguishable from a covered-up leak.
#
# Fingerprints are commit:path:rule:line, so an entry stops applying the moment the
# line moves. That is deliberate: a re-review is cheap, a stale blanket exemption is
# not. Never add a path glob here — a rule that cannot see test files cannot catch
# the real secret somebody eventually pastes into one.
#
# NOTE: describe offending values, never reproduce them. A comment quoting the
# literal string re-introduces it in a new commit, and the scanner is right to
# flag that too.

